    {
      "filename": "Alfred Jacob Miller - Storm - Waiting for the Caravan - Walters 371940147.jpg",
      "title": "File:Alfred Jacob Miller - Storm - Waiting for the Caravan - Walters 371940147.jpg",
      "url": "https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/5/56/Alfred_Jacob_Miller_-_Storm_-_Waiting_for_the_Caravan_-_Walters_371940147.jpg",
      "descriptionUrl": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Alfred_Jacob_Miller_-_Storm_-_Waiting_for_the_Caravan_-_Walters_371940147.jpg",
      "width": 1800,
      "height": 1273,
      "mime": "image/jpeg",
      "license": "Public domain",
      "artist": "Alfred Jacob Miller",
      "description": "One of Miller's most beautifully painted and atmospheric pictures, \"Storm\" shows those who have gone ahead in a driving rainstorm and are waiting for the rest of the train to catch up. Miller said that after two or three days of rain he would become depressed, causing the captain to suggest that his \"early training\" had been \"faulty.\"",
      "dateCreated": "between 1858 and 1860<div style=\"display: none;\">date QS:P571,+1850-00-00T00:00:00Z/7,P1319,+1858-00-00T00:00:00Z/9,P1326,+1860-00-00T00:00:00Z/9</div>",
